WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.020
- Practice faithful persistence

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:04.400
means never ever ever give up.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:05.400
I mean how many of you

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.400
have ever had a great idea,

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.390
talked about it, thought
about it, didn't do it

00:00:08.390 --> 00:00:09.630
and then someone else did it.

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:10.710
And was successful

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.960
and you went darn I should have done that.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:12.960
you know one of the greatest myths

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.480
that's pervasive in our culture today

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.970
is that you're entitled to a great life.

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:18.340
If you're not experiencing joy

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.440
as you as you think about doing something

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:21.650
and as you pursue doing it

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:24.150
then it's off course for you.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.410
- He's an American author,

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:27.500
motivational speaker, corporate trainer

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:28.500
and entrepreneur.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:29.640
He's the co-author

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.400
of the Chicken Soup for the Soul series

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.390
that has sold over five
hundred million copies

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:36.080
in 40 languages.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:38.870
In 2005 he co-authored
the success principles

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:40.390
How to Get from Where You Are

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:41.930
to Where you Want to Be.

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:43.100
He's Jack Canfield

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.100
and here is my take

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.620
on his top ten rules for success.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.340
Rule number one is my personal favorite.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:48.450
I'm curious to find out

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:49.690
which one you guys like the best.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:51.380
also as you're watching the video

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:52.780
if you hear something that Jack says

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:53.780
that really resonates with you

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:56.010
add it to the comments with quotes

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:57.010
so we can keep track

00:00:57.010 --> 00:01:01.829
of what you find most relevant.

00:01:01.829 --> 00:01:03.780
- Practice faithful persistence

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.290
means never ever ever give up.

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:07.670
Chicken Soup for the Soul

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:11.110
was rejected by 144 publishers.

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:12.540
144 publisher said

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:13.540
we don't want to publish

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.280
a collection of short stories.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:17.420
The title's stupid
Chicken Soup for the Soul.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:18.490
What does that mean?

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:21.670
People don't buy collections
of short stories.

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:23.400
There's never been you know successful

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.650
chain of doing that.

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:28.650
So literally we spent 14 months

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.090
trying to find a publisher

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:32.110
and we go to New York with our agent

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:34.110
and eventually our agent
gave us the book back

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:36.020
and said I can't sell this.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:37.020
So we went

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:38.340
to the National Booksellers Association

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:40.040
convention down in Anaheim.

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:41.770
We went from booth to booth to booth

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:43.250
for three days.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:45.930
And there were 4,000
publishers represented there

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:47.420
and we go would you publish our book?

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:49.420
Would you publish our book?

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:51.060
And we got no, no, no, no, no.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:52.320
It was late on the third day

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.970
that a little publisher from Florida

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:56.390
after we'd gotten over 144 rejections

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:57.810
said we'll read it

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:00.250
and then we said well how many copies

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:01.250
do you think we'll sell

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:02.250
after they said yeah we'll buy it.

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:03.710
A couple weeks later he
said we'll publish it.

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:07.130
And they said well maybe
20,000 if we're lucky.

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:09.220
Now we said our goal is to sell a million

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:11.290
and a half in a year and a half.

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:12.730
Now have you ever told someone your dream

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:14.247
and had them laugh out loud at you?

00:02:14.247 --> 00:02:15.980
(audience laughs)

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:17.970
He laughed out loud.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:19.360
Now if we had given up

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:21.300
after a hundred publishers had said no

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.930
I wouldn't be standing here today.

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:25.330
You know, wouldn't have happened.

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:27.760
And so you've got to
be willing to persevere

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:29.860
because we didn't take no.

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:30.860
See when the world says no

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:32.540
you say next.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:34.640
Let's practice that if I say no you say...

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:35.640
- [Audience] Next.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:36.640
- Absolutely there's only five

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:38.290
or six billion people out there.

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:39.830
You can go and ask right.

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:41.540
There's over four thousand publishers

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:43.750
just here in the state of California.

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:46.060
So what we have is this
endless possibility

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:47.060
but you have to persevere.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:50.200
It's as if the universe
tests our commitment.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:53.150
And so today we have 147 titles in print.

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:55.220
We sold over 115 million copies.

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:57.260
We're in 47 languages

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:58.810
and over a billion dollars worth

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:00.320
of Chicken Soup for the Soul books

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:01.480
have been sold worldwide.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:04.430
So if you're willing to
decide what you want,

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:05.870
believe it's possible,

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:08.120
consciously envision the future,

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:09.620
feel the feelings of
what it would feel like

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.510
if you'd achieve this goal.

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:12.790
You can have anything

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:14.350
and then you take action

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:15.870
both obvious actions

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:16.900
and inspired actions.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:19.020
You can do anything.

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:21.090
One of the functions of belief

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:22.600
is taking action.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:25.010
We did a survey of about
2,000 top entrepreneurs

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:26.620
and we noticed that one of the things

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:28.540
that people who win in that world have

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:30.380
is a bias for action.

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:32.500
If they have an
inspiration they act on it.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:33.500
I mean how many of you

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:34.750
have ever had a great idea,

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:36.400
talked about it, thought
about it, didn't do it

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:37.870
and then someone else did it.

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:38.880
And was successful

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:40.790
and you went darn I should have done that.

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:42.800
Maybe it was by that piece of property.

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:43.840
We all have that piece of property

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:46.540
we wish we'd bought you know.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:48.370
Anyway so we're going to be looking at

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:49.910
the idea that taking action

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:50.950
is part of the Law of Attraction.

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:52.290
See a lot of people think

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:53.730
you just sit in your room,

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:54.990
meditate, visualize,

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:56.790
having the perfect car, the perfect house,

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:57.910
the perfect relationship

00:03:57.910 --> 00:03:59.710
and then it'll kind of just come to you.

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:00.710
And I always say

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:02.160
unless you live at the bottom of the hill

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:03.160
(audience laughs)

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:05.730
where there's a road

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:06.910
there's probably not
going to be a Cadillac

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:09.360
show up in your living room right.

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:10.650
So think about this.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.200
The last six letters

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.370
of the word attraction spell what?

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:16.950
A, C, T, I, O, N, action.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:18.190
Now there's two kinds of actions

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:19.570
that are critical.

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:20.640
There's obvious actions.

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:22.230
If you want a certain kind of car

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:24.000
you should go down and test drive it.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.850
You should find out how much it costs.

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:28.290
You should see what it
costs to maintain it.

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:30.100
You should go you know spend...

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:32.100
I like to test drive a
car three or four times

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:33.260
go down to the dealer,

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:34.260
take a camera,

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:35.260
stick my head out the window.

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:36.260
Say take a picture of me.

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:37.260
(audience laughs)

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:38.260
I'll be back to buy it.

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:39.400
Put it up on my refrigerator.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.560
Look at it every day.

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:42.560
Eventually you know

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:44.260
those kind of things produce car.

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:45.760
Right saving for it and so forth

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:46.850
but there are also things

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:48.960
called inspired actions.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:50.380
All of a sudden you get an inspiration

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:51.380
to do something

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:53.620
and you didn't know what it was.

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:54.620
You don't have a sense

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:56.260
of like how's this rationally
going to make sense

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:58.050
for me to move forward in my life.

00:04:58.050 --> 00:04:59.980
I'll give you an example a friend of mine

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:01.480
Dr. Ignatius Piazza

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:03.660
graduates chiropractic school.

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:05.900
He wants to move to
Monterrey near Pebble Beach

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:07.210
where the golf course is

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:08.210
and he gets there

00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:10.380
and he says to the local
Chiropractic Association

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:11.380
like to join you,

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:12.720
and like you to help me
get my practice started.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:13.720
And they said

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:14.760
we don't need any more chiropractors.

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:15.760
We have one chiropractor

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:17.830
for every eight people in this area.

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:19.040
It's too many.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:20.160
Now he could have said okay

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:21.790
let the external reality control

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:23.030
his internal experience.

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:24.450
But he doesn't do that he said

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:26.710
I'm going to think about this

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:28.270
and visualize it and believe in it

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:30.450
and something will come that I will do.

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:31.980
And what came to him to do

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:33.120
was to take six months

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:34.860
before he opened his office

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:36.640
and put a pin where he wanted his office

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:38.330
and then concentric circles

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:40.270
knock on every door in every neighborhood

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:41.810
saying Hi I'm a new doctor in town

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:43.680
could I ask you a few questions.

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:44.800
You know I'm starting this practice

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:47.550
should I open from 5:00
to 9:00 in the morning

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:48.610
and or should I be open

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:49.840
from 5:00 until 9:00 at night

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:51.600
for people who have nine-to-five jobs.

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:52.860
Which would be better?

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:54.240
Should I advertise in this paper

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:55.240
or that paper?

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:56.960
Should I call it Ignatius
Piazza chiropractic

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:58.900
or chiropractic West?

00:05:58.900 --> 00:05:59.900
Then his last question was

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:00.900
if I have an open house

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:02.310
would you like to receive an invitation?

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:03.510
They said yes.

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:04.630
He wrote it down.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:05.800
Now over six months he knocked

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:08.390
on 12,500 doors,

00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:10.680
talk to 6,500 people

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:12.460
and gathered over 4,000 names

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:13.460
of people who said yes

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:15.990
I'd like an invitation to your open house.

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:17.940
Now when he opened his
office six months later

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:19.100
in a town that did not need

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:20.440
another chiropractor according

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:21.820
to the professionals

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:23.250
his first month in practice

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:26.800
he netted $72,000.

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:28.090
In his first year in practice

00:06:28.090 --> 00:06:31.430
his gross income was
over a million dollars.

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:32.430
I was giving a talk

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:33.530
and mentioned this story

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:34.530
just about five years ago

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:37.550
and this happened about 25 years ago.

00:06:37.550 --> 00:06:39.290
Someone said he knocked on my door.

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:42.528
(audience laughs)

00:06:42.528 --> 00:06:44.090
And he left his card

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:45.820
and two years later I
needed the chiropractor

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:46.820
and I called him

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:48.240
because we work with people we know,

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:49.790
we've had an experience with right.

00:06:49.790 --> 00:06:50.870
So he trusted his intuition.

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:52.740
He took action on it.

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:53.740
Other people would say

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:56.190
oh if I can't have what I want.

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:58.350
You got to be willing to take the action.

00:06:58.350 --> 00:06:59.610
If you're going to be successful

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:01.550
in creating the life of your dreams

00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:02.580
you have to believe that

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:05.570
you are capable of making it happen.

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:07.600
You have to believe that
you have the right stuff

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:09.780
and that you're able to pull it off.

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:11.810
Now whether you call it self-esteem,

00:07:11.810 --> 00:07:13.790
self-confidence or self assurance,

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:15.460
it's a deep-seated belief

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:17.050
that you have what it takes,

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:19.300
the abilities, the inner resources,

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:20.820
the talents and the skills

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:23.060
to create your desired results.

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:24.570
Now believing in yourself

00:07:24.570 --> 00:07:26.590
is simply an attitude.

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:28.860
Believing yourself is a choice.

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:30.440
You have to choose to believe

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:33.630
that you can do anything
you set your mind to.

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:35.050
Anything at all

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:36.980
because in fact you can.

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:37.980
It might help you to know

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:40.570
that the latest brain
research now indicates

00:07:40.570 --> 00:07:42.070
with enough positive self-talk

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:44.080
and positive visualization

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:45.990
combined with proper training, coaching,

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:48.030
and practice anyone can learn

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:50.040
to do almost anything.

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:51.160
Now I've interviewed thousands

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:52.740
of successful people

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:53.740
and almost every one of them

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:56.170
has told me I was not the most gifted

00:07:56.170 --> 00:07:58.530
or the most talented person in my field

00:07:58.530 --> 00:08:02.020
but I chose to believe
that anything was possible.

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:03.610
And because of that I studied,

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:04.940
I practiced and I worked harder

00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:05.940
than the others

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:07.820
and that's how I got to where I am.

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:09.300
You know if Ruben Gonzalez,

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:11.930
a 20 year old living in Texas,

00:08:11.930 --> 00:08:14.170
hot Texas can pick up the luge

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:15.490
which is a winter sport

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:17.570
and become an Olympic athlete,

00:08:17.570 --> 00:08:20.380
if Bill Gates who is a college dropout

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:22.760
can become a multi-billionaire

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:23.850
and Stephen Jay Cannel

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:25.620
who was a dyslexic student

00:08:25.620 --> 00:08:27.880
who failed three grades in school

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:29.290
can become a best-selling author

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:31.150
and a television producer

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:33.120
then you too can accomplish anything

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:35.840
if you'll simply believe it's possible.

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:37.220
So make the decision right now

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:40.930
to believe that you create
all of your experiences

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:42.250
because you do.

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:44.060
Let's start creating the ones you want

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:45.210
by believing you can.

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:47.140
Sounds a little strange

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:49.580
but accepting this level of responsibility

00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:51.970
is uniquely and inevitably empowering.

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:54.820
It means you can do, change

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:56.210
and become anything at all.

00:08:56.210 --> 00:08:57.820
You may think that something as small

00:08:57.820 --> 00:08:58.970
as being optimistic

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:00.570
won't change much about your life.

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:02.620
Have you ever heard this line?

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:03.620
Just because I'm paranoid

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:05.450
doesn't mean the world
isn't out to get me.

00:09:05.450 --> 00:09:06.770
Now that may be a joke

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:08.200
but many people believe

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:10.300
the deck is stacked against them.

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:12.000
People who are reverse paranoids

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:13.900
otherwise known as optimists

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:16.160
use the same consistent thinking

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:17.600
but they believe that
the world is plotting

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:19.680
to do them good.

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:21.040
Everything that happens is pushing them

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:22.480
in the right direction.

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:24.310
This attitude breeds more good thoughts

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:25.380
so why not practice

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:27.480
to become a reverse paranoid?

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:29.350
Start seeing obstacles as opportunities

00:09:29.350 --> 00:09:31.450
to grow and change.

00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:32.450
When your presentation

00:09:32.450 --> 00:09:33.650
doesn't get the sale

00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:34.660
see it as an opportunity

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:36.450
to create a better presentation

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:38.540
and become better at your job.

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:39.540
See the task

00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:40.540
that gives you some power

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:42.080
to change rather than the fear

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:43.870
that makes you feel powerless.

00:09:43.870 --> 00:09:45.580
Look for the seed of something better

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:47.880
when everything is going wrong.

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:49.420
Almost everyone sees getting laid off

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:51.140
as a bad thing but even

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:52.590
if you want your job to be over

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:55.440
the end always feel sad and uninspiring.

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:56.680
The end of one job however

00:09:56.680 --> 00:09:58.000
always holds the promise

00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:59.330
of the new beginning,

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:00.510
of the next job.

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:01.510
If you look at it that way

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:02.580
you're focusing on what

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:04.890
a reverse paranoid thinks about.

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:08.690
Identify the great benefit in every event.

00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:09.690
Soon you'll start to see

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:11.010
that good is not an accident

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:12.760
but something you create
with your attitudes.

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:14.560
Walk through your home,

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:15.790
your business, your apartment,

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:18.140
your condo, anything you're in charge of

00:10:18.140 --> 00:10:20.600
and make a list of all the things

00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:22.470
that aren't exactly the way you wanted.

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:24.860
There's never a stapler
by the Xerox machine.

00:10:24.860 --> 00:10:26.800
Someone always leaves that cabinet open.

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:28.580
My kid never picks up after himself.

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:29.860
Those pictures are always slanted.

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:31.060
They never stay straight.

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:32.260
The screen door slams.

00:10:32.260 --> 00:10:33.260
There's a hole in the window.

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:35.370
You know whatever it is write it down

00:10:35.370 --> 00:10:36.370
and then go back

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:37.440
and here's the key part.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:38.490
Remember in law of attraction

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:39.880
we always it's on what you want

00:10:39.880 --> 00:10:41.390
not what you don't want.

00:10:41.390 --> 00:10:42.390
You don't want to be going

00:10:42.390 --> 00:10:43.390
I don't want a man who smokes.

00:10:43.390 --> 00:10:44.940
I don't want a man who
watches TV all weekend.

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:46.640
I don't want a man who...

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:47.640
(audience laughs)

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:48.910
Because that's what you're going to get.

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:51.080
Alright because what you focus on

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:52.080
is what you attract.

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:53.840
So you want to focus on the opposite.

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:54.950
So what you want to focus on

00:10:54.950 --> 00:10:57.080
is the opposite of your irritation list.

00:10:57.080 --> 00:10:59.290
There'll always be a stapler
by the Xerox machine.

00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:01.190
We solved it in our
office with a little chain

00:11:01.190 --> 00:11:02.333
and some glue.

00:11:02.333 --> 00:11:04.040
(audience laughs)

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:06.310
It doesn't leave, okay.

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:07.920
But the key is there's always solutions.

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:09.770
The pictures that won't stay straight.

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:10.960
Velcro right to the wall.

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:11.960
Go on the bottom.

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:12.960
It works you know

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:14.100
but the point is

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:15.100
you want to get a list

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:16.760
of what's the outcome you want

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:18.220
and then take a day

00:11:18.220 --> 00:11:21.010
hire person or you know
bring a friend over

00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:22.370
and go through the list

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:23.630
and get as many done as you can.

00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:25.010
You know all the easy ones.

00:11:25.010 --> 00:11:26.300
Build some momentum.

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:27.300
Clean the garage.

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:28.300
Develop a new filing system.

00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:29.430
That might be something you'd you know

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:31.220
set off to another weekend.

00:11:31.220 --> 00:11:32.220
And we say all the big ones

00:11:32.220 --> 00:11:33.220
that are really big

00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:34.700
do one a quarter every, three months,

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:35.700
solve one of those.

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:37.270
Now you're getting rid of
all the stuff in your life

00:11:37.270 --> 00:11:38.380
and why is this so important.

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:40.240
We're talking mostly about being wealthy,

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:41.510
having great relationships,

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:43.690
great health, world peace, ending hunger,

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:46.480
and you're talking about the screen door.

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:48.270
When you don't fix the screen door

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:49.520
you settle.

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:50.870
And when you settle consistently

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:52.330
you develop a habit of settling

00:11:52.330 --> 00:11:53.850
for what you don't want.

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:56.660
And most people go through
life in resignation.

00:11:56.660 --> 00:11:57.660
They've resigned themselves

00:11:57.660 --> 00:11:59.290
to not having it the way they want it.

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:02.500
It's taking no less
than 100% responsibility

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:04.080
for your life.

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:05.080
You know one of the greatest myths

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:07.040
that's pervasive in our culture today

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:09.020
is that you're entitled to a great life

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:11.300
and then somehow somewhere someone

00:12:11.300 --> 00:12:13.830
is responsible for filling our lives

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:15.200
with continual happiness

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:16.620
and exciting career options,

00:12:16.620 --> 00:12:18.010
a nurturing family

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:20.240
and blissful personal relationships

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:22.360
simply because we exist

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:24.050
but the real truth is

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:25.850
that there's only one person responsible

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:27.660
for the quality of your life

00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:29.990
and that person is you.

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:31.620
You see everything about you

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:34.270
is a result of your doing or not doing.

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:37.330
Your income, your debt,
your relationships,

00:12:37.330 --> 00:12:39.930
your health, your fitness
level, your attitudes

00:12:39.930 --> 00:12:42.420
and behaviors, everything.

00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:43.420
That person you see

00:12:43.420 --> 00:12:44.870
when you look in the mirror

00:12:44.870 --> 00:12:47.950
is the chief architect in your life.

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:49.270
You know I think everybody knows this

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:50.270
in their heart of hearts

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:52.190
but the mind can play games

00:12:52.190 --> 00:12:53.380
tricking us into thinking

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:55.200
that there are external factors

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:57.160
that are the source of our failures,

00:12:57.160 --> 00:12:59.820
our disappointments and our unhappiness.

00:12:59.820 --> 00:13:01.220
But the truth of the matter

00:13:01.220 --> 00:13:02.810
is that external factors

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:05.850
don't determine how you live.

00:13:05.850 --> 00:13:08.010
You and only you are

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:09.450
in complete control of the quality

00:13:09.450 --> 00:13:12.290
of your life experience.

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:14.270
Successful people take full responsibility

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:16.050
for the thoughts they think,

00:13:16.050 --> 00:13:17.700
the images they visualize

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:19.230
and the actions they take.

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:20.680
They don't waste their time

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:23.100
and energy on blaming and complaining.

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:24.630
They evaluate their experiences

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:27.260
and decide if they need
to change them or not.

00:13:27.260 --> 00:13:29.160
They face the uncomfortable

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:30.160
and they take risks

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:31.180
in order to create the life

00:13:31.180 --> 00:13:32.640
that they want to live.

00:13:32.640 --> 00:13:33.640
How many of you

00:13:33.640 --> 00:13:34.640
have ever complained in your life?

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:35.640
(audience laughs)

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:36.830
Yeah you know.

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:39.660
Here's what I've learned
about complaining.

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:40.740
In order to complain

00:13:40.740 --> 00:13:42.220
I have to have a reference point

00:13:42.220 --> 00:13:43.840
of something better that I want

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:46.060
that I'm not willing to risk creating.

00:13:46.060 --> 00:13:47.270
Now let me explain that again.

00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:49.540
I have to have a
reference point in my mind

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:50.610
of something I want

00:13:50.610 --> 00:13:52.170
that's better than what I have

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:54.140
that I'm not willing to risk creating.

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:56.510
So what I do is complain about it instead.

00:13:56.510 --> 00:13:59.330
See if I was complaining about my wife

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:00.920
it would mean that I would have to believe

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:02.190
that somewhere out there in the world

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:04.450
there's a better woman than my wife.

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:07.790
See if every woman on the planet died

00:14:07.790 --> 00:14:08.790
except my wife

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:11.360
do you think I'd go to work the next day

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:12.360
and complain about her?

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:13.360
(audience laughs)

00:14:13.360 --> 00:14:14.810
No, she's the only one.

00:14:14.810 --> 00:14:17.102
(audience laughs)

00:14:17.102 --> 00:14:18.320
And I'd be going hey and I got her.

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:20.060
This is really cool right?

00:14:20.060 --> 00:14:21.360
(audience laughs)

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:24.260
Do you ever hear anyone
complain about gravity?

00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:26.480
(audience laughs)

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:27.480
Very rarely.

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:28.480
You know gravity makes us all bent over.

00:14:28.480 --> 00:14:29.480
Do you ever see an old person

00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:30.520
walking down a street going,

00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:31.520
gravity.

00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:32.520
They have a little walker.

00:14:32.520 --> 00:14:33.520
I hate gravity.

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:34.520
(audience laughs)

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:35.520
If it weren't for gravity

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:38.140
I wouldn't be all bent over like this.

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:39.140
Gravity sucks.

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:40.140
(audience laughs)

00:14:40.140 --> 00:14:41.870
Now have you ever heard

00:14:41.870 --> 00:14:43.290
an older person doing that?

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:45.970
No, the reason they don't
complain about gravity

00:14:45.970 --> 00:14:48.480
is because there's no alternative to it.

00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:50.490
You know gravity just is.

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:52.360
So if someone's
complaining about something

00:14:52.360 --> 00:14:53.430
it means they know

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:55.410
there's something they can do about it

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:56.490
because we don't complain

00:14:56.490 --> 00:14:58.830
about the things we can't change.

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:00.970
So as soon as you hear
yourself complaining

00:15:00.970 --> 00:15:02.330
I want you to stop

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:04.670
and say okay what would I rather have?

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:05.970
remember Law of Attraction

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:07.600
always just focus on what you want

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:09.170
not what you don't want

00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:10.170
because when you're talking about

00:15:10.170 --> 00:15:11.170
what you don't want,

00:15:11.170 --> 00:15:12.170
when you're complaining and blaming

00:15:12.170 --> 00:15:13.450
you're focusing on

00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:14.760
that which you don't want

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:16.900
and you're accelerating its expression

00:15:16.900 --> 00:15:17.930
out into the universe

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:19.990
with those negative feelings.

00:15:19.990 --> 00:15:21.270
And yet we'll spend a majority

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:23.040
of our time complaining

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:25.420
about so many things.

00:15:25.420 --> 00:15:26.930
And usually we complain about them

00:15:26.930 --> 00:15:28.820
to people who can't do anything about it.

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:30.310
Make a list of 101 things

00:15:30.310 --> 00:15:32.470
you want to achieve before you die.

00:15:32.470 --> 00:15:33.830
Now I was sharing this
with someone last night.

00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:34.830
He said God that just seems

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:35.830
like a really big task.

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:36.830
I'm a single mom.

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:37.758
I don't have any time.

00:15:37.758 --> 00:15:39.279
When am I going to do that?

00:15:39.279 --> 00:15:42.112
(audience laughs)

00:15:42.950 --> 00:15:44.210
We know that one of the things

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:45.270
about high achievers

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:46.890
is that they all have goals.

00:15:46.890 --> 00:15:49.610
Only 10% of Americans
set goals every year.

00:15:49.610 --> 00:15:50.610
10%.

00:15:50.610 --> 00:15:51.610
I go to sales confrences,

00:15:51.610 --> 00:15:52.820
people that learn this stuff,

00:15:52.820 --> 00:15:53.920
hear it over and over.

00:15:53.920 --> 00:15:54.920
How many?

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:55.920
10%.

00:15:55.920 --> 00:15:57.320
We also know the same three

00:15:57.320 --> 00:16:01.090
to 10% control 90% of the
resources in the world.

00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:03.250
So literally without goals
you're directionless.

00:16:03.250 --> 00:16:04.250
You will be used.

00:16:04.250 --> 00:16:05.250
See people without goals

00:16:05.250 --> 00:16:07.880
get used by other people who have them.

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:08.880
People that don't have goals

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:10.620
work for people who do.

00:16:10.620 --> 00:16:11.830
And so you want to be someone

00:16:11.830 --> 00:16:13.480
who picks up and gets clear

00:16:13.480 --> 00:16:14.890
about what you want.

00:16:14.890 --> 00:16:15.890
Make a list.

00:16:15.890 --> 00:16:16.890
101 goals.

00:16:16.890 --> 00:16:17.890
I want to go to Paris.

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:18.890
I want to you know skydive.

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:20.290
I want to bungee cord jump.

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:21.860
I want to play the guitar.

00:16:21.860 --> 00:16:23.110
I want to learn to juggle.

00:16:23.110 --> 00:16:25.290
I want to learn two magic
tricks for the kids.

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:27.690
I want to go to the Olympics in Beijing.

00:16:27.690 --> 00:16:29.500
Whatever it is make the list.

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:31.450
And you'll see there's a
lot of stuff under there

00:16:31.450 --> 00:16:33.730
that you've kind of put down that you want

00:16:33.730 --> 00:16:35.500
and you can have anything you want.

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:36.810
If you want to know how to decide

00:16:36.810 --> 00:16:38.420
if a career opportunity is a good one

00:16:38.420 --> 00:16:39.420
there are several things

00:16:39.420 --> 00:16:40.810
you have to take into consideration.

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:43.440
Number one, does it make your heart sing.

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:45.100
The number one feedback system

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:47.760
that you are given at birth is joy.

00:16:47.760 --> 00:16:48.980
If you're not experiencing joy

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:51.070
as you as you think about doing something

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:52.870
and as you pursue doing it

00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:54.720
then it's off course for you.

00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:56.870
You also want to put your
rational mind to work.

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:59.120
You want to some due diligence.

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:00.120
Ask other people

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:01.630
who've gone down that road before.

00:17:01.630 --> 00:17:02.870
What was it like?

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:03.870
What did they have to do?

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:06.150
What were some of the costs of that path?

00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:07.150
What were some of the pay offs

00:17:07.150 --> 00:17:08.470
and the benefits?

00:17:08.470 --> 00:17:09.470
And really get a sense

00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:11.680
of what it would be like to do that.

00:17:11.680 --> 00:17:12.680
Sometimes you can go

00:17:12.680 --> 00:17:13.940
and do an internship

00:17:13.940 --> 00:17:15.730
or you can work for a
friend in their restaurant

00:17:15.730 --> 00:17:17.140
just to see if you like it

00:17:17.140 --> 00:17:18.230
because often the fantasy

00:17:18.230 --> 00:17:19.990
doesn't match the reality.

00:17:19.990 --> 00:17:21.690
And the other thing is

00:17:21.690 --> 00:17:25.030
to simply trust yourself.

00:17:25.030 --> 00:17:27.390
You know deep inside what's true for you

00:17:27.390 --> 00:17:29.080
and if you'll take a few minutes

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:31.450
and go inside, we call it meditation,

00:17:31.450 --> 00:17:33.580
and just ask and sit with the question

00:17:33.580 --> 00:17:35.730
and see what kind of feelings come up.

00:17:35.730 --> 00:17:36.730
Does this feel right?

00:17:36.730 --> 00:17:39.130
So do all the rational research

00:17:39.130 --> 00:17:40.370
but then ultimately bring it back

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:42.340
into your heart and decide

00:17:42.340 --> 00:17:44.010
does this feel good for me?

00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:45.080
And if it makes sense up here

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:46.240
and it feels good

00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:47.750
then step into it.

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:49.840
Just lean into it and see what happens.

00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:50.950
Pursue it.

00:17:50.950 --> 00:17:52.370
No decision is forever.

00:17:52.370 --> 00:17:53.370
You can always change

00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:54.960
if it's not what you want.

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:56.460
When you're a kid

00:17:56.460 --> 00:17:58.820
you have an impulse to act, you act.

00:17:58.820 --> 00:17:59.850
You want to touch the cat,

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:01.250
you want to throw the cat out the window,

00:18:01.250 --> 00:18:03.480
you want to stick your hand into the VCR,

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:05.240
and put peanut butter in there, you do.

00:18:05.240 --> 00:18:06.240
The problem is

00:18:06.240 --> 00:18:07.240
as we're growing up

00:18:07.240 --> 00:18:09.380
we get conditioned by our parents

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:11.480
and our caretakers and our siblings

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:12.580
and our teachers and coaches

00:18:12.580 --> 00:18:14.270
and nuns and all these different people

00:18:14.270 --> 00:18:15.640
that come into our life,

00:18:15.640 --> 00:18:16.640
don't do that.

00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:17.640
Stop, that's bad.

00:18:17.640 --> 00:18:18.640
You know we get slapped

00:18:18.640 --> 00:18:19.640
and told we're not OK.

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:20.730
And so after a while

00:18:20.730 --> 00:18:21.830
when we go to do something

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:24.200
we're looking, is it ok if I do this.

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:27.090
You know instead of just doing it.

00:18:27.090 --> 00:18:28.710
All my sons and my stepson

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:29.710
and my stepdaughter

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:31.170
have been great risk takers.

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:32.510
They're all artists.

00:18:32.510 --> 00:18:34.070
One's a drummer.

00:18:34.070 --> 00:18:35.290
One's a hip-hop singer.

00:18:35.290 --> 00:18:37.640
One is in high school

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:39.000
but he's in the school play.

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:41.470
He just had to lead in the school play.

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:42.470
He's a singer.

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:43.500
And then my daughter's a singer

00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:45.500
and my other son is very athletic.

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:47.390
He's a surfer.

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:48.950
He snow boards as well

00:18:48.950 --> 00:18:50.710
and he's always inventing games

00:18:50.710 --> 00:18:52.010
and trying out new things.

00:18:52.010 --> 00:18:53.320
Always on the edge you know.

00:18:53.320 --> 00:18:55.260
Always coming in with cuts and scrapes

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:56.260
which I love

00:18:56.260 --> 00:18:58.110
because they're out there on the edge

00:18:58.110 --> 00:18:59.580
of their potential, exploring

00:18:59.580 --> 00:19:00.790
how they can keep pushing it.

00:19:00.790 --> 00:19:02.280
And it's not that they never get scared

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:03.470
or they never feel rejected

00:19:03.470 --> 00:19:04.890
and have to go through things.

00:19:04.890 --> 00:19:08.890
But they seem to rebound very quickly.

