00:20:00.420 --> 00:20:04.869
- The other thing,

00:20:04.869 --> 00:20:05.860
a friend of mine just wrote a book

00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:09.510
called The Fear Cure or the Cure for fear,

00:20:09.510 --> 00:20:10.510
one of those.

00:20:10.510 --> 00:20:12.000
And she talked about

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:13.020
one of the biggest fears

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:15.200
is of the unknown and
uncertainty of the future

00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:17.880
but everything is uncertain.

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:19.600
You know we're trying to create certainty

00:20:19.600 --> 00:20:20.630
in an uncertain world

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:22.760
and stop being afraid of uncertainty.

00:20:22.760 --> 00:20:23.760
Uncertainty is what's exciting.

00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:26.630
You go to Africa on a vacation, a safari.

00:20:26.630 --> 00:20:28.290
You've no idea what's going to happen.

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:29.290
That's part of the adventure.

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:30.290
- It's fun.

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:31.290
- That's part of the fun exactly.

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:32.290
- If you knew all there's
going to be a zebra

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:33.290
that pops out right here

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:34.290
or this is going to be next

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:35.290
that would be boring right.

00:20:35.290 --> 00:20:36.290
- Or if you go river rafting

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:37.300
you don't know where the rapids are

00:20:37.300 --> 00:20:38.340
and how you're going to do it

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:39.340
and if you go surfing

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:40.340
you don't know exactly how the wave

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:41.390
is going to break and all that

00:20:41.390 --> 00:20:42.480
and how big it's going to be.

00:20:42.480 --> 00:20:46.210
And so that adventure is
really what life's about

00:20:46.210 --> 00:20:47.840
and so we need to be excited.

00:20:47.840 --> 00:20:50.850
Fear is created by imagining bad things

00:20:50.850 --> 00:20:52.340
that haven't happened yet.

00:20:52.340 --> 00:20:54.610
So fantasized experiences appearing real.

00:20:54.610 --> 00:20:55.780
Everyone always says that.

00:20:55.780 --> 00:20:56.780
Someone else recently said

00:20:56.780 --> 00:20:58.080
forget everything and run.

00:20:58.080 --> 00:21:00.520
But I think that if you realize

00:21:00.520 --> 00:21:02.510
that you're creating your own fear

00:21:02.510 --> 00:21:03.870
by imagining a bad thing,

00:21:03.870 --> 00:21:05.490
of if there's a recession
I'll lose my house.

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:07.380
Why not go if there was a recession

00:21:07.380 --> 00:21:08.440
I'm going to make more money

00:21:08.440 --> 00:21:09.700
because there's going to be opportunities

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:12.500
and we're going to be able
to pay our house out faster.

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:14.830
Zig Ziglar said worrying

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:16.590
is negative goal-setting

00:21:16.590 --> 00:21:17.630
and all you have to do

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:19.450
is use that same power to think

00:21:19.450 --> 00:21:21.620
and visualize to create a positive outcome

00:21:21.620 --> 00:21:22.750
instead of a negative

00:21:22.750 --> 00:21:24.650
and then the fear disappears.

00:21:24.650 --> 00:21:25.650
Let's look at this idea

00:21:25.650 --> 00:21:27.850
of specificity for a minute.

00:21:27.850 --> 00:21:29.410
Like a winter home in Hawaii.

00:21:29.410 --> 00:21:30.820
Very nice

00:21:30.820 --> 00:21:32.900
but if I say I will own

00:21:32.900 --> 00:21:34.260
a two-bedroom beachfront villa

00:21:34.260 --> 00:21:36.750
on the west coast of Maui Hawaii

00:21:36.750 --> 00:21:39.610
by June 1st 2003

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:41.990
does that sound a little more clear?

00:21:41.990 --> 00:21:44.570
Yeah and until you get specific like that

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:46.240
the creative part of your brain

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:47.780
won't jump in

00:21:47.780 --> 00:21:50.260
and decide how to help you get there.

00:21:50.260 --> 00:21:51.260
And that's why a lot of people

00:21:51.260 --> 00:21:52.260
never get their dreams

00:21:52.260 --> 00:21:55.010
because they don't make
them specific enough.

00:21:55.010 --> 00:21:57.410
You got to get real nitty-gritty.

00:21:57.410 --> 00:21:59.620
Break it down.

00:21:59.620 --> 00:22:00.640
How much buy when?

00:22:00.640 --> 00:22:02.970
I want a better relationship
with my husband.

00:22:02.970 --> 00:22:05.170
What does that mean?

00:22:05.170 --> 00:22:07.040
But if I say I want to
spend an hour a week

00:22:07.040 --> 00:22:08.300
sitting opposite my husband

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:12.220
talking about real things that matter,

00:22:12.220 --> 00:22:13.340
no TV on,

00:22:13.340 --> 00:22:15.550
eye to eye communication,

00:22:15.550 --> 00:22:16.780
well that we can measure.

00:22:16.780 --> 00:22:18.480
Did you do it for an hour?

00:22:18.480 --> 00:22:20.420
Want to have more fun.

00:22:20.420 --> 00:22:21.420
What does that mean?

00:22:21.420 --> 00:22:22.420
Well, what if I say I'm going to listen

00:22:22.420 --> 00:22:23.820
to comedy albums twice a week

00:22:23.820 --> 00:22:25.330
for a minimum of an hour.

00:22:25.330 --> 00:22:26.840
You're probably going to have more fun.

00:22:26.840 --> 00:22:28.280
So make it specific make it.

00:22:28.280 --> 00:22:29.830
Make it real.

00:22:29.830 --> 00:22:30.830
Some people say you know

00:22:30.830 --> 00:22:31.830
I want our business to increase.

00:22:31.830 --> 00:22:33.440
Well how much by when?

00:22:33.440 --> 00:22:35.100
Want the reading scores
to go up in a school.

00:22:35.100 --> 00:22:36.480
How much, by when?

00:22:36.480 --> 00:22:37.640
Until you have that

00:22:37.640 --> 00:22:38.640
you're not going to make progress

00:22:38.640 --> 00:22:39.870
and so many people's dreams

00:22:39.870 --> 00:22:41.260
never get completed

00:22:41.260 --> 00:22:42.260
because they're not clear

00:22:42.260 --> 00:22:44.010
about the specific number

00:22:44.010 --> 00:22:45.390
of how much by when.

00:22:45.390 --> 00:22:47.480
I told you earlier in the program.

00:22:47.480 --> 00:22:48.590
We said we're going to sell a million

00:22:48.590 --> 00:22:50.460
and a half books in a year and a half

00:22:50.460 --> 00:22:53.290
and that directed our behavior.

00:22:53.290 --> 00:22:54.290
Recently we just said

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:56.530
we're going to sell a
million books in one day.

00:22:56.530 --> 00:22:57.720
We had 101 bookstores

00:22:57.720 --> 00:22:59.550
involved in a book signing.

00:22:59.550 --> 00:23:00.570
I'm going to try to be

00:23:00.570 --> 00:23:01.720
in the Guinness Book of World Records

00:23:01.720 --> 00:23:03.720
for the largest book signing ever done.

00:23:03.720 --> 00:23:05.340
Now I don't think we sold a million books.

00:23:05.340 --> 00:23:06.340
Maybe we sold

00:23:06.340 --> 00:23:08.130
a couple hundred thousand

00:23:08.130 --> 00:23:09.940
but by holding that question

00:23:09.940 --> 00:23:11.210
and trying to figure out how to do it

00:23:11.210 --> 00:23:12.770
it moved us toward that goal.

00:23:12.770 --> 00:23:13.770
Now maybe it'll take us two years

00:23:13.770 --> 00:23:15.360
to figure out how to sell a million books

00:23:15.360 --> 00:23:16.360
in one day

00:23:16.360 --> 00:23:17.360
but it gets the thinking

00:23:17.360 --> 00:23:19.100
to expand out into that arena.

00:23:19.100 --> 00:23:20.370
Is this making sense?

00:23:20.370 --> 00:23:22.750
Okay so you want to have those goals.

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:23.880
Now the other thing you want to do

00:23:23.880 --> 00:23:26.260
is break your goals down.

00:23:26.260 --> 00:23:27.720
Many of you have big goals,

00:23:27.720 --> 00:23:29.630
end hunger in the world.

00:23:29.630 --> 00:23:30.800
That's a pretty big goal.

00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:32.160
You know have world peace.

00:23:32.160 --> 00:23:35.130
Achieve a certain level
of spiritual oneness

00:23:35.130 --> 00:23:36.940
with God or life.

00:23:36.940 --> 00:23:37.940
Big goals.

00:23:37.940 --> 00:23:40.700
When you first look at
it's kind of overwhelming

00:23:40.700 --> 00:23:41.700
but what if we were to break that down

00:23:41.700 --> 00:23:43.170
into little steps

00:23:43.170 --> 00:23:44.610
that says okay I want to go to college

00:23:44.610 --> 00:23:45.610
and get a PhD.

00:23:45.610 --> 00:23:47.340
Gosh I'm only a high school student

00:23:47.340 --> 00:23:48.850
but the next step would be

00:23:48.850 --> 00:23:50.110
finish the math class.

00:23:50.110 --> 00:23:51.370
Get an A in this.

00:23:51.370 --> 00:23:53.350
Write for a brochure from a college.

00:23:53.350 --> 00:23:54.970
Get a catalog.

00:23:54.970 --> 00:23:56.080
Pick one or five colleges

00:23:56.080 --> 00:23:57.480
that I want to apply to.

00:23:57.480 --> 00:23:58.880
You know just keep breaking it down

00:23:58.880 --> 00:24:00.480
to little steps and then figure out

00:24:00.480 --> 00:24:01.640
how to get all those steps done

00:24:01.640 --> 00:24:03.630
and put a date by each step.

00:24:03.630 --> 00:24:05.460
And then start doing the plan.

00:24:05.460 --> 00:24:06.770
Someone said if you fail to plan

00:24:06.770 --> 00:24:08.160
you're planning to fail.

00:24:08.160 --> 00:24:09.530
Does that make sense?

00:24:09.530 --> 00:24:10.530
Yeah absolutely.

00:24:10.530 --> 00:24:12.100
Some of one of my friends

00:24:12.100 --> 00:24:14.480
said success by the yard is hard

00:24:14.480 --> 00:24:15.890
by the inch it's a cinch.

00:24:15.890 --> 00:24:18.290
So we just break it
down into small pieces.

00:24:18.290 --> 00:24:19.980
I had I was reading

00:24:19.980 --> 00:24:21.040
the Guinness Book of World Records

00:24:21.040 --> 00:24:22.470
cause we were thinking
about being in there

00:24:22.470 --> 00:24:24.490
and this guy set a goal

00:24:24.490 --> 00:24:26.370
to eat an entire bicycle.

00:24:26.370 --> 00:24:28.010
(audience gasps)

00:24:28.010 --> 00:24:29.520
Tires and all.

00:24:29.520 --> 00:24:31.720
Now how do you do that?

00:24:31.720 --> 00:24:34.670
right well it took him 17 days

00:24:34.670 --> 00:24:35.670
but what he did is

00:24:35.670 --> 00:24:36.750
he kept cutting the bicycle up

00:24:36.750 --> 00:24:37.780
and then melting it down

00:24:37.780 --> 00:24:39.340
into little swallowable pieces

00:24:39.340 --> 00:24:40.340
and he ate them.

00:24:40.340 --> 00:24:42.400
I don't know how much stayed in

00:24:42.400 --> 00:24:43.990
but he ate them right?

00:24:43.990 --> 00:24:45.000
But the point being

00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:46.090
anything can be done

00:24:46.090 --> 00:24:47.980
if you break it down small enough.

00:24:47.980 --> 00:24:49.020
Make sense?

00:24:49.020 --> 00:24:50.020
So don't let the bigness

00:24:50.020 --> 00:24:51.510
of a goal overwhelm you.

00:24:51.510 --> 00:24:52.940
Now I was over in Bangkok.

00:24:52.940 --> 00:24:53.940
How many of you've been

00:24:53.940 --> 00:24:55.280
to Bangkok Thailand.

00:24:55.280 --> 00:24:57.150
How many of you have
seen the Golden Buddha?

00:24:57.150 --> 00:24:59.160
It's one of the three tourist attractions.

00:24:59.160 --> 00:25:00.170
You always see the Jade Buddha,

00:25:00.170 --> 00:25:01.870
the Golden Buddha and the Reclining Buddha

00:25:01.870 --> 00:25:02.870
and that kind of thing

00:25:02.870 --> 00:25:03.900
and this Buddha is 10

00:25:03.900 --> 00:25:07.080
and a half feet tall of solid gold.

00:25:07.080 --> 00:25:10.880
The gold value alone is
about 196 million dollars.

00:25:10.880 --> 00:25:12.640
That doesn't even count the artistic

00:25:12.640 --> 00:25:14.220
and the historical value.

00:25:14.220 --> 00:25:17.260
And when my wife was taking that picture

00:25:17.260 --> 00:25:19.170
I was over next to the

00:25:19.170 --> 00:25:20.290
I'd say about five feet away

00:25:20.290 --> 00:25:22.200
there was a big glass case

00:25:22.200 --> 00:25:23.200
and in that case

00:25:23.200 --> 00:25:24.200
there was a piece of clay

00:25:24.200 --> 00:25:27.400
about a foot wide, two
feet tall, two feet thick

00:25:27.400 --> 00:25:30.010
and it said that in 1953

00:25:30.010 --> 00:25:31.420
they did not know there was such a thing

00:25:31.420 --> 00:25:33.000
as a Golden Buddha.

00:25:33.000 --> 00:25:34.660
They were moving this large clay Buddha

00:25:34.660 --> 00:25:35.840
from one side of Bangkok

00:25:35.840 --> 00:25:38.470
to the other to make room for a

00:25:38.470 --> 00:25:39.760
road that was coming through.

00:25:39.760 --> 00:25:41.290
And as they picked up the Buddha

00:25:41.290 --> 00:25:42.760
with the crane because it was very heavy

00:25:42.760 --> 00:25:44.590
a big crack went down through it.

00:25:44.590 --> 00:25:46.350
And as the crack went down through it

00:25:46.350 --> 00:25:47.980
the head monk got scared

00:25:47.980 --> 00:25:49.210
and he lowered the Buddha down.

00:25:49.210 --> 00:25:51.170
And he said you know we'd better

00:25:51.170 --> 00:25:52.230
take a look at it and see

00:25:52.230 --> 00:25:53.800
if we've done any damage to it

00:25:53.800 --> 00:25:54.800
and it started to rain

00:25:54.800 --> 00:25:56.090
so they put a canvas over it

00:25:56.090 --> 00:25:57.670
to keep it dry.

00:25:57.670 --> 00:25:58.880
That night the monk came out

00:25:58.880 --> 00:26:00.510
and he shined a flashlight in

00:26:00.510 --> 00:26:01.540
to see if we was staying dry

00:26:01.540 --> 00:26:02.890
and something reflected back

00:26:02.890 --> 00:26:04.840
from inside the crack.

00:26:04.840 --> 00:26:06.440
He said clay does not reflect light.

00:26:06.440 --> 00:26:08.220
There must be something else in there.

00:26:08.220 --> 00:26:09.250
And so the next morning

00:26:09.250 --> 00:26:10.580
they chipped away in behind

00:26:10.580 --> 00:26:11.580
where they wouldn't see it

00:26:11.580 --> 00:26:12.580
if they've made a mistake

00:26:12.580 --> 00:26:13.580
and lo and behold

00:26:13.580 --> 00:26:16.070
sure enough was this Golden Buddha.

00:26:16.070 --> 00:26:17.980
And their best theory is

00:26:17.980 --> 00:26:19.150
that three hundred years earlier

00:26:19.150 --> 00:26:21.670
when the Burmese were attacking Thailand

00:26:21.670 --> 00:26:23.040
the monks of this monastery

00:26:23.040 --> 00:26:24.300
covered up the Golden Buddha

00:26:24.300 --> 00:26:26.580
with clay to make it look worthless

00:26:26.580 --> 00:26:28.270
so they wouldn't steal it.

00:26:28.270 --> 00:26:30.760
They also think all the monks were killed

00:26:30.760 --> 00:26:31.950
in a massacre

00:26:31.950 --> 00:26:36.129
and the secret died with the monks.

00:26:36.129 --> 00:26:37.450
And then they'd rediscovered it.

00:26:37.450 --> 00:26:38.980
The word discover means what?

00:26:38.980 --> 00:26:40.720
Take the cover off of.

00:26:40.720 --> 00:26:41.720
Discover something.

00:26:41.720 --> 00:26:43.090
It was always in there

00:26:43.090 --> 00:26:44.150
but they took the cover off.

00:26:44.150 --> 00:26:46.400
I was having dinner
with my wife that night

00:26:46.400 --> 00:26:47.400
and she said

00:26:47.400 --> 00:26:48.640
you know Jack that Buddha

00:26:48.640 --> 00:26:50.990
is like all the people in our seminars.

00:26:50.990 --> 00:26:53.330
They come in with this cover of clay

00:26:53.330 --> 00:26:54.710
of their negative beliefs,

00:26:54.710 --> 00:26:56.860
their self-doubt, their sense

00:26:56.860 --> 00:26:59.080
of guilt and shame, their beliefs

00:26:59.080 --> 00:27:00.110
that they're not enough,

00:27:00.110 --> 00:27:01.110
that they're not worthy,

00:27:01.110 --> 00:27:02.580
they don't deserve and

00:27:02.580 --> 00:27:03.580
and what we really do

00:27:03.580 --> 00:27:04.700
is we take the clay off

00:27:04.700 --> 00:27:06.620
so this golden essence can come

00:27:06.620 --> 00:27:09.030
and be there as who they are again.

00:27:09.030 --> 00:27:10.030
They're true identity.

00:27:10.030 --> 00:27:12.220
It's not like we put anything in.

00:27:12.220 --> 00:27:13.990
It's just that we remove the things

00:27:13.990 --> 00:27:14.990
that are not there.

00:27:14.990 --> 00:27:15.990
I think Barbara talked a little

00:27:15.990 --> 00:27:17.910
about that earlier today.

00:27:17.910 --> 00:27:20.240
So as we go through this
next hour and a half

00:27:20.240 --> 00:27:22.820
think about and hold that metaphor.

00:27:22.820 --> 00:27:24.450
That image of the Buddha

00:27:24.450 --> 00:27:25.940
and it could be the golden Christ,

00:27:25.940 --> 00:27:27.540
the Golden Buddha, the Atman,

00:27:27.540 --> 00:27:29.580
the source, whatever you want to call it,

00:27:29.580 --> 00:27:31.050
but that's who you really are.

00:27:31.050 --> 00:27:32.050
And although we do

00:27:32.050 --> 00:27:34.080
a lot of things of giving
you more information

00:27:34.080 --> 00:27:35.710
and tools and all of that

00:27:35.710 --> 00:27:37.320
really if you were to stop

00:27:37.320 --> 00:27:38.980
doing the stuff that's negative

00:27:38.980 --> 00:27:41.630
as Harp said you've been defined,

00:27:41.630 --> 00:27:43.300
when you came in you were just fine,

00:27:43.300 --> 00:27:44.630
and what we did was we layered

00:27:44.630 --> 00:27:45.630
on all that stuff.

00:27:45.630 --> 00:27:48.470
If we could just start to remove that

00:27:48.470 --> 00:27:50.610
and realize that everything you need

00:27:50.610 --> 00:27:51.880
is in you now.

00:27:51.880 --> 00:27:53.020
You have everything you need

00:27:53.020 --> 00:27:54.980
to do everything you want to do.

00:27:54.980 --> 00:27:58.980
It's just that we've
learned not to trust that.

